 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? In Italian, it roughly translates to, how much is it going to cost me? You' still use vedova, but now it's just you and your partner. Say c'e fu far concentello, which means it was worth the money. Fun to play with. Ask for the bill in advance, and keep a ticket or small note. If you forget, ask the busiest guest. You' picked up on the small detail that makes you look polite and confident. It makes a big difference.",
